## Why This Is Asked

Tests diagnosing certificate rotation within a service mesh, focusing on end-to-end TLS verification, per-tenant isolation, and zero-downtime deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts

- TLS certificate rotation propagation across Kubernetes secrets and Envoy proxies
- mTLS handshake troubleshooting in Istio service mesh
- Canary rollouts with automated rollback capabilities
- Per-tenant routing and isolation in multi-tenant mesh environments

## Code Example

```javascript
// TLS handshake tester (pseudo)
async function testTLS(target) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(target);
    return response.ok;
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor certificate expiration dates across all pods?
- What metrics would you use to detect TLS handshake failures in real-time?
- How do you ensure tenant isolation during certificate rotation?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests deep production debugging skills, including multi-tenant cache management, Redis eviction policies, and safe rollout procedures under traffic.

## Key Concepts
- Redis eviction policies (volatile-lru, allkeys-lru, etc.) and TTL management
- Multi-tenant namespace isolation in Redis using key prefixes
- Canary rollout strategies (e.g., Argo Rollouts or manual phased deployments)
- Observability: Redis INFO metrics, hit/miss ratios, and application latency metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify current eviction policy
const evictionPolicy = await redis.configGet('maxmemory-policy');
console.log('Current eviction policy:', evictionPolicy);

// Check keyspace stats
const info = await redis.info('stats');
const hits = info.match(/keyspace_hits:(\d+)/)[1];
const misses = info.match(/keyspace_misses:(\d+)/)[1];
const hitRate = hits / (hits + misses);
console.log('Hit rate:', hitRate);
```
